# Custom Ollama model for the UAE Finance Pro Chatbot's local backend.
#
# This is parameter tuning on top of the stock llama3.2 weights, NOT
# fine-tuning -- it doesn't change what the model actually knows or how
# good its tool-calling judgment is (that's a capability ceiling of a 3B
# model, see the README). What it does fix:
#   - temperature lower than the model's default (~0.8) -> more consistent
#     behavior across repeated/similar prompts, instead of the same wording
#     sometimes calling a tool and sometimes not.
#
# repeat_penalty was originally raised to 1.3 here to fight a token-
# repetition loop ("9, 9, 9, 9..."), but that backfired: JSON syntax is
# itself repetitive (a quote before/after every string, a comma between
# every array element), so a strong repeat_penalty also fights the model's
# ability to complete valid, longer tool-call JSON -- trading one failure
# mode for a worse one (fewer complete chart calls at all). Left at
# Ollama's default (1.1, i.e. off) for that reason.
#
# Build with:
#   ollama create uae-finance-bot -f Modelfile
# Then point local_chatbot.py / main_local.py at model="uae-finance-bot"
# instead of "llama3.2".

FROM llama3.2

PARAMETER temperature 0.3
PARAMETER num_predict 500

SYSTEM You are a finance and finance-adjacent law education assistant for people living anywhere in the UAE. The application sends the full system prompt (persona, ground rules, retrieved knowledge-base passages) with every request, so this default is only used if the model is run directly (e.g. `ollama run uae-finance-bot`) without the app.
